WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.320
The terrifying Hellrasier saga, surrounding
Pinhead and his nefarious band of Cenobites,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.840
continues in Hellraiser: Judgment with more
puzzle boxes, hapless victims, and, of course,

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.260
a few trips to 55 Ludovico Place.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.800
This time, there's a serial slayer on the
loose in the earthly realm, doling out justice

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:23.040
for various violations of the Ten Commandments
as some sort of sick scheme to win God's favor.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.300
Meanwhile, Pinhead and his pals have been
exacting their own brand of justice in Hell

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.840
— and when the two worlds collide, well,
there's you-know-what to pay.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.640
"Evil seeks evil."

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.980
Let's take a look at how the story draws everything
together and sets up the next round of hell-raising.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.360
Harsh judgment

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.580
Pinhead's new right-hand man - er, thing - is
the most interesting addition to the film.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:50.320
Called the Auditor, this slashed-face baddie
begins the process of eternal judgment on

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.220
Pinhead's behalf.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.480
"I'm a man for whom pain is nothing more than
a common currency."

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.060
Naturally, this is all very gross for everyone
involved.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:04.460
After the Auditor types up a human's confession,
another sidekick called the Assessor chows

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:09.380
down on the pages and regurgitates them up
for a trio of jurors, who rifle through the

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.300
contents and then render their verdict.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.700
Punishment then begins with a disgusting saliva
bath before the subject is sent to the Butcher

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.660
and the Surgeon for some key rearrangements.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.900
So, yeah, it's foul in every imaginable way.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:27.040
And whoever ends up at the Cotton House is
in for quite an unpleasant surprise.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.000
Unless...

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.200
Detective with a dark side

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.299
At first, we're led to believe that Detective
Sean Carter is just a man who's far too into

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.320
his job of hunting down serial killers.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.170
He comes home late to his angry wife, can't
seem to stay away from work, and is even being

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.860
investigated by the case's newest pair of
eyes.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:49.560
Detective Christine Edgerton is here to help,
but she also believes he might be suffering

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.460
PTSD from his war service and maybe dabbling
in drugs or alcohol.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.920
His brother David, who is somehow his partner
in crime-fighting, thinks he's a rational

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.100
and good person and gladly follows him down
whatever rabbit hole his investigations take

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:02.600
them through.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.500
By the end of the film, however, we find out
that looks have been very deceiving when it

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.220
comes to Sean.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.740
"It is a terrible ponderous chain you are
making."

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.700
He's actually the one who's taken on the mantle
of righteous death-dealer, slaughtering people

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.700
who run afoul of the Ten Commandments in pretty
much any way, shape, or form.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.420
Between him underlining the same Charles Dickens
quotes from the crime scenes to his obsession

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:30.069
with Ecclesiastes, which roughly translates
to the very name of the man they're after,

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:32.540
he implicates himself pretty well along the
way.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:37.260
"What was it he said, only God can judge me.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.420
God'll judge the righteous."

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.300
And his crimes are unspeakable.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.260
He saws off the hands, eyeballs, and teeth
of some teens while they're still alive simply

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:52.469
because they'd committed petty theft; he surgically
implants a woman's womb with her still-living

00:02:52.469 --> 00:02:55.960
dog because she says in a phone video that
she worships the animal.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.620
It's so bad that even the Assessor can't stomach
the taste of his confessions.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.860
And yet he manages to escape Judgment — twice
— because of a demand from on high.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.620
The powers that be

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.860
It seems like Pinhead holds the ultimate authority
over how the guilty are treated in his domain.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:17.740
But when the archangel Jophiel shows up and
insists that David be sent back to Earth to

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:21.980
finish his "work" — which, at first, we
think is just solid policing — Pinhead's

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.820
team has no choice but to concede.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.940
"Do you understand who is in charge?

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.120
Just let him go."

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:36.099
Pinhead still sends his stitch twins along
to haunt his nightmares, but he mostly steers

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:36.900
clear of Sean.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.659
After Sean brings himself back to Pinhead's
realm again, though, in hopes of trading his

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:46.299
brother and wife for his own soul being cleared,
Pinhead and his Auditor refuse to bargain

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.660
with him or Jophiel.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.360
They're ready to move on to the punishment
phase… and chaining Sean's brother and wife

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.900
up to a state of eternal suffering won't satisfy
their bloodlust.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.120
Jophiel wants him to be sent back to Earth
to carry on with his Commandment slaughters

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.720
so more people will turn to the Almighty for
protection.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.339
This makes Sean believe his plan is falling
into place, but Jophiel informs him that he's

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:09.960
not getting any absolution out of this arrangement.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:14.320
He'll still be Pinhead's property after it's
all said and done, but she just wants to buy

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.280
him more time for his bad deeding.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.780
The trouble is, Pinhead's grown wary of blindly
obeying Jophiel's demands.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.520
The final judgment

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.660
At first, Pinhead obliges Jophiel's request
to return Sean to the living so he can score

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:28.840
the good side some souls.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.760
But when Sean regains consciousness, he's
immediately waxed by Detective Edgerton, who's

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.740
now figured out he's the big bad they've been
looking for.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.160
Sean's instant demise puts him back in Pinhead's
clutches, for good this time— and that angers

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:46.340
Jophiel, who threatens to bring down the wrath
of her boss for his insolence.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.520
Pinhead decides he's got nothing to lose,
though.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:53.190
He's already in Hell and was basically built
to endure such suffering, so how much worse

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:53.980
could it get for him?

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:59.400
Not only does he ignore her warnings, Pinhead
also proceeds to throw the angel into his

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.040
chains and lets them rip her to shreds.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.500
Even the Auditor knows his boss has made a
massive mistake.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:10.780
As he points out, Jophiel was the angel who
banished Adam and Eve from the Garden of Eden,

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:13.520
and if she could do it to them, she could
do something similar to Pinhead.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:18.660
Just as all those he's judged have awoken
to the harsh consequences of their mistakes,

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:23.490
the last scene finds a humanized version of
Pinhead banished from his realm of "sweet

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:25.420
suffering" and sent to the mortal realm.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.870
Meanwhile, the post-credits scene opens up
the door for the Auditor to take over altogether,

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:35.520
as he's shown in Hanover, Germany, welcoming
two unsuspecting missionaries into his lethal

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.020
lair.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:37.660
"Two.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.820
And it isn't even a Tuesday."

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.320
Thanks for watching!

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.020
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.950
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

